00:12:26.905 --> 00:12:30.030
a use case like this,
and I think, you know,

00:12:30.030 --> 00:12:32.430
it requires a certain level
of maturity that I would say,

00:12:32.430 --> 00:12:34.510
like, early on in our
journey we maybe didn't have,

00:12:34.510 --> 00:12:37.965
but we were kinda lucky in certain
ways is You need to be very,

00:12:38.585 --> 00:12:41.145
direct with the business
and make them understand that,

00:12:41.145 --> 00:12:43.645
like, look, we can build this.
We can build this very quickly.

00:12:44.250 --> 00:12:47.850
And it's fun to do to
build, but it will require maintenance.

00:12:47.850 --> 00:12:50.970
And maintenance means there
is cost associated to that.

00:12:50.970 --> 00:12:55.385
So we need to make sure
that whatever they're asking for has

00:12:55.385 --> 00:12:56.665
benefits, right,

00:12:56.665 --> 00:13:00.345
like actual tangible benefits so that
when we do go back to

00:13:00.345 --> 00:13:02.340
them and say, like,
look, I to, you know,

00:13:02.340 --> 00:13:05.640
assign like an FTE to kinda
do long term support for this.

00:13:06.500 --> 00:13:09.445
They're okay with
funding. Right?

00:13:09.445 --> 00:13:11.445
So that part is very
important. And, you know,

00:13:11.445 --> 00:13:14.405
we need to be very direct
about that very upfront, right?

00:13:14.405 --> 00:13:16.965
Which is why a lot of the
use cases that we we tend to

00:13:16.965 --> 00:13:19.120
support their
fairly high value.

00:13:19.120 --> 00:13:20.320
And when they're
very high value,

00:13:20.320 --> 00:13:22.480
you go back to them and
you're like, look, I can build this.

00:13:22.480 --> 00:13:24.100
It'll cost you next to nothing.

00:13:24.720 --> 00:13:26.960
For support, we need to
kind of support this,

00:13:26.960 --> 00:13:30.335
and that will kinda have
some costs. Typically,

00:13:30.335 --> 00:13:32.175
they're they're
they're okay with that.

